<p>The Board of Peace is pursuing two Gaza-related tracks reflected in the source reports: talks with Hamas on a possible disarmament arrangement and discussions with Dubai-based DP World on a possible logistics role in reconstruction. Lead envoy Nickolay Mladenov told Reuters in Brussels on April 20 that he was “fairly optimistic” an arrangement could eventually work for all sides, while warning that the discussions with Hamas have been difficult and that progress needs to come quickly. On reconstruction, the Financial Times reported that the board reviewed a proposal under which DP World would manage supply chains and logistics as part of a US plan for the devastated enclave. The effort comes as global institutions estimate Gaza’s rehabilitation could cost about $70 billion, with roughly four-fifths of buildings reported destroyed after two years of Israeli bombardment.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/l5GYhgu2OFgJQ9FaBBUU2uStwyLqlf_459kG7xAoFVxHg9_8KkEYR38r03wTngAm1At2h8BrBKt_Nc3V4S-kRk5n7TPX9lQzSquSHK6ECzXl9cCV_uzlyw1Nhw4ObtsvQRQryj0P5wV1EJa3cTLf3ddkZbYpoA8l1rIV_D6RUK4HUTZ8tG2gOFwCOwv7wwgTKa5l554tcUJ1n1-D5C4P1oPwLR5fgq6LRZ8C6-Dyy6YE8GwaGnbbCrF83iN6Z0ZCwC8a3HdqzaDhTpQ0xQ' alt='DP World-related image accompanying report on talks over a logistics role in Gaza reconstruction' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Brussels talks: Mladenov gave the update during a visit to Brussels, saying the board had held “very serious discussions” with Hamas in recent weeks.</li><li>Logistics focus: The reported DP World talks centered on a potential partnership to handle logistics and supply chains, not a broader reconstruction mandate.</li><li>Emirati role: DP World is an Emirati company, making the proposal notable because it could give a Gulf logistics operator a central operational role in postwar Gaza rebuilding.</li><li>Time pressure: The envoy said quick progress matters even though a final arrangement will still take time, underscoring the gap between diplomatic momentum and real-world implementation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Nickolay Mladenov: The envoy struck a cautiously optimistic tone, saying a disarmament plan for Hamas and other militant groups could be reached, while stressing that negotiations remain difficult and unfinished. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/board-peace-envoy-says-gaza-plan-needs-quick-progress-hamas-talks-not-easy'>Al-Monitor/Reuters</a>)</li><li>Board of Peace: The board reviewed a proposal that would use outside commercial logistics support, with DP World discussed as a possible operating partner for Gaza supply chains. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/873b866b-fd17-426d-8cb1-a34566e2e1d4'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>DP World: The reported talks focused on whether the company could take on a logistics-management role in Gaza’s rebuilding effort rather than any broader political role. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trumps-board-of-peace-holds-talks-with-dp-world-on-rebuilding-gaza-ft-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/board-of-peace-envoy-says-gaza-plan-needs-quick-progress-hamas-talks-not-easy'>Board of Peace envoy says Gaza plan needs quick progress, Hamas talks ‘not easy’</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/board-peace-envoy-says-gaza-plan-needs-quick-progress-hamas-talks-not-easy'>Board of Peace envoy says Gaza plan needs quick progress, Hamas talks &#x27;not easy&#x27;</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/873b866b-fd17-426d-8cb1-a34566e2e1d4'>Trump’s ‘Board of Peace’ held talks with DP World over Gaza reconstruction</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/donald-trumps-board-of-peace-held-talks-with-dp-world-over-gaza-reconstruction-report/article70887241.ece'>Donald Trump’s ‘Board of Peace’ held talks with DP World over Gaza reconstruction: report</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>